---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../../components/ContactCTA.astro';

const title = 'Drain Cleaning in Albert Lea, MN | A-1 Drain Cleaning';
const description = 'A-1 Drain Cleaning provides 24/7 drain cleaning and sewer-line service in Albert Lea, Minnesota for clogged drains, backups and stopped main lines. Call 641-530-2728.';
const phone = '641-530-2728';
---

<MainLayout title={title} description={description} path="/service-area/albert-lea-mn/">
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="bg-[#1A1A68] py-14 text-white sm:py-20 lg:py-24">
      <div class="container">
        <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-300"><a href="/" class="hover:text-white">Home</a><span class="mx-2" aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/service-area/" class="hover:text-white">Areas We Serve</a><span class="mx-2" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span class="text-white">Albert Lea</span></nav>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-red-300">Albert Lea, Minnesota</p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-4xl text-5xl font-black leading-[.98] tracking-tight sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl">Drain Cleaning in Albert Lea, MN</h1>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-200 sm:text-xl">A-1 Drain Cleaning serves Albert Lea with 24/7 drain and sewer-line service. If one drain is stopped, several fixtures are backing up, or wastewater is coming up through a floor drain, call and describe the pattern.</p>
        <a href="tel:+16415302728" class="call-button mt-8 inline-block rounded-md bg-[#c52b34] px-7 py-4 text-center text-lg font-black text-white shadow-lg hover:bg-[#a82129]">CALL 641-530-2728</a>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-300">24/7 service • Albert Lea • Drain cleaning • Main drain clearing • Sewer-line blockages</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <figure class="bg-white py-8 sm:py-10">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl overflow-hidden rounded-xl shadow-xl">
          <img src="/images/sewer-drain-mason-city-iowa.jpg" alt="Josh Theilen operating a sewer drain cleaning machine" width="663" height="1142" loading="eager" decoding="async" class="block h-auto max-h-[620px] w-full object-cover object-center sm:max-h-[680px]" />
        </div>
        <figcaption class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-5xl text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">A-1 Drain Cleaning owner Josh Theilen working on a main sewer drain. A-1 provides drain and sewer service for Albert Lea and surrounding communities.</figcaption>
      </div>
    </figure>

    <section class="bg-white py-14 sm:py-18"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-4xl"><p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Albert Lea drain problems</p><h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">The symptom pattern matters</h2><p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">A single slow sink, a toilet that will not clear, and several fixtures backing up together are not the same situation. A-1 uses the details you provide to determine what kind of drain or sewer service is appropriate.</p></div><div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"><article class="border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6"><h3 class="text-2xl font-black">One sink, tub, or shower</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">A single slow fixture can be a local restriction. Tell us whether it is slow, completely stopped, or intermittently clears.</p></article><article class="border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6"><h3 class="text-2xl font-black">Several fixtures at once</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">When sinks, toilets, tubs, or floor drains are affected together, the restriction may be farther down a shared drain or main line.</p></article><article class="border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6"><h3 class="text-2xl font-black">Sewer backup</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">If wastewater is rising through a floor drain, tub, or shower, limit water use rather than repeatedly testing the line.</p></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="bg-slate-100 py-14 sm:py-18"><div class="container grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.2fr_.8fr]"><div><p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Common Albert Lea calls</p><h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">When the drain problem is bigger than one fixture</h2><p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">A main drain or sewer-line restriction can show up in different ways depending on the home. In a basement, wastewater may rise through the floor drain. In a home without a basement, the tub or shower may be the lowest visible fixture.</p><p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">Pay attention to what triggers the backup. If a toilet flush makes a tub rise, or the washing machine discharge sends water toward a floor drain, stop adding water and tell A-1 exactly what happened.</p></div><aside class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-7"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">A-1 service options</h2><nav class="mt-5 grid gap-3" aria-label="Related drain services"><a class="font-black text-[#b4232b] underline" href="/services/">All drain & sewer services</a><a class="font-black text-[#b4232b] underline" href="/services/main-drain-cleaning/">Main Drain Cleaning</a><a class="font-black text-[#b4232b] underline" href="/services/sewer-line-cleaning/">Sewer Line Cleaning</a><a class="font-black text-[#b4232b] underline" href="/services/sewer-backup-emergency/">Sewer Backup Emergency Service</a><a class="font-black text-[#b4232b] underline" href="/services/tree-roots-in-sewer-line/">Tree Roots in Sewer Lines</a><a class="font-black text-[#b4232b] underline" href="/drain-problem-quiz/">Drain Problem Troubleshooter</a></nav></aside></div></section>

    <section class="bg-white py-14 sm:py-18"><div class="container max-w-5xl"><p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Drain backup checklist</p><h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">What to do when wastewater is backing up</h2><div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><article class="border-l-4 border-[#c52b34] bg-slate-50 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black">1. Limit water use</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">Do not keep flushing toilets or running sinks, showers, and laundry to test a line that is already backing up.</p></article><article class="border-l-4 border-[#c52b34] bg-slate-50 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black">2. Keep people away from sewage</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">Keep children and pets away from contaminated wastewater and avoid unnecessary contact with the affected area.</p></article><article class="border-l-4 border-[#c52b34] bg-slate-50 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black">3. Do not pour chemical opener</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">Chemical drain products are not a substitute for clearing a backed-up main drain and can create a hazardous situation for anyone working on the line.</p></article><article class="border-l-4 border-[#c52b34] bg-slate-50 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black">4. Explain the sequence</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">Tell us which fixture was affected first, what happened when another fixture was used, and whether the problem has happened before.</p></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="bg-[#1A1A68] py-14 text-white sm:py-18"><div class="container text-center"><p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-red-300">24/7 drain service</p><h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-black sm:text-5xl">Need drain cleaning in Albert Lea?</h2><p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-200">Call A-1 Drain Cleaning at 641-530-2728. We will start with the symptoms, location of the backup, and what the plumbing does when water is used.</p><a href="tel:+16415302728" class="mt-7 inline-block rounded-md bg-[#c52b34] px-8 py-4 text-lg font-black text-white">CALL A-1: 641-530-2728</a></div></section>
  </main>
  <ContactCTA />
  <Footer />
</MainLayout>
